{"content":[{"c":["GOLAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City and a district in the territory given to Manasseh in Bashan. It was the northernmost city of refuge east of the Jordan River (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.43","r":"Deut.4.43","rawR":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.43","value":"Deut.4.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 4:43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.20.8","r":"Josh.20.8","rawR":"Josh.20.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.20.8","value":"Josh.20.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 20:8"},"), given to the Levite family of Gershon (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.27","r":"Josh.21.27","rawR":"Josh.21.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.27","value":"Josh.21.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.71","r":"1Chr.6.71","rawR":"1Chr.6.71","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.71","value":"1Chr.6.71"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:71"},"). Of uncertain identification, it was known to Josephus as a fertile area, and to Eusebius as a village. The best current suggestion places it at Sehem el-Jolan, east of the river el-’Allan."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CitiesofRefuge_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cities of Refuge"},"; ",{"href":"?item=LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LeviticalCities_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Levitical Cities"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Golan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 4:43","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.43","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.43","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.43"},{"anchorText":"Jos 20:8","canonicalization":"deferr